  "payload": {
   "provider": "Dr. Meghan Adams",
   "specialty": "gastroenterology",
   "page_count": 2,
   "pages": [
    {
     "page": 1,
     "text": "**CLINICAL SUMMARY - Buckley Group Medical Group**\n\n**Patient:** Kristi Wilson **DOB:** 02/27/2008 **Sex:** F **MRN:** 848033\n\n**Encounters:**\n- **2026-07-01:** Patient presented with concerns related to cirrhosis. Blood pressure was recorded at 114/85 mmHg, and weight was 126 lbs. The patient reported feeling well otherwise with no new symptoms or complications. Laboratory tests confirmed controlled cirrhosis with stable liver function tests.\n \n- **2026-01-21:** Follow-up visit for cirrhosis. BP was 112/87 mmHg, and weight was 131 lbs. Physical exam was unremarkable, and no signs of decompensation were noted. Liver enzymes remained within normal limits, indicating stable disease. The patient continues to adhere to dietary and lifestyle recommendations.\n\n- Routine check-up for cirrhosis management. BP was 114/89 mmHg, and weight was 122 lbs. The patient reported no new complaints and appeared well. Abdominal ultrasound and other imaging studies confirmed no progression of cirrhosis. Continued adherence to prescribed lifestyle modifications.\n\n- **2025-03-04:** Cirrhosis follow-up. BP was l24/92 mmHg, and weight was 119 lbs. Physical exam revealed no new findings, and the patient remained asymptomatic. Liver function tests showed stable liver function without evidence of decompensation. Patient education on the importance of ongoing monitoring and lifestyle management was reinforced.\n\n- **2024-09-23:** Initial diagnosis of cirrhosis. BP was 116/91 mmHg, and weight was 128 lbs. Liver biopsy confirmed cirrhosis. The patient was educated on disease management, including dietary restrictions, avoidance of alcohol, and regular follow-up visits. Initial lab results indicated mild elevation in liver enzymes which have since stabilized.\n\n**Assessment/Plan:**\n- **Cirrhosis:** The patient has been diagnosed with cirrhosis, which is currently under control with no evidence of decompensation. There have been no changes in her medical management plan. The patient is compliant with dietary and lifestyle recommendations aimed at managing her condition. There are no prescribed medications for cirrhosis at this time.\n\n- **Social History:** The patient is a current cigarette smoker with a usage of one pack per day. She has been honest about her tobacco use, and counseling on smoking cessation has been provided during each visit. \n\nAdditionally, the patient has no history of alcohol use. She has a family history that is unremarkable for liver disease.\n\n**Vital Signs:**\n- **2026-07-01:** BP 114/85, Wt 126 lbs\n- **2026-01-21:** BP 112/87, Wt 131 lbs\n- **2025-0"
    },
    {
     "page": 2,
     "text": "8-12:** BP 114/89, Wt 122 lbs\n- **2025-03-04:** BP 124/92, Wt 119 lbs\n- **2024-09-23:** BP 116/91, Wt 128 lbs\n\n**Physical Exam:**\n- **2026-07-01:** Unremarkable; no jaundice, no ascites, no splenomegaly.\n- **2026-01-21:** Unremarkable; no jaundice, no ascites, no splenomegaly.\n- **2025-08-12:** Unremarkable; no jaundice, no ascites, no splenomegaly.\n- **2025-03-04:** Unremarkable; no jaundice, no ascites, no splenomegaly.\n- **2024-09-23:** Unremarkable; no jaundice, no ascites, no splenomegaly.\n\n**Follow-Up:**\nThe patient is advised to continue regular follow-up visits every 3-6 months to monitor the status of her cirrhosis. She should adhere to dietary restrictions and avoid alcohol. Smoking cessation support and counseling will continue to be offered at each visit. \n\n---\n\nThis summary includes all relevant clinical information, structured visit details, assessment, and plan for the patient, Kristi Wilson, as requested.\n"
